1949:
** ἐπιλαμβάνω**,
**take** or **get besides**, ἐπὶ τοῖς πεντήκοντα ταλάντοις ἑκατόν 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Politica” 1259a28: with _genitive_ _partitive_, ἐ. τοῦ χρόνου **take a little more** time, {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|M.Ant. 1.17; τῆς ἀρχῆς 2nd c.AD: Pausanias Periegeta 9.14.5.}}
**2**. simply, **take, receive**, {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|“PEleph.” 10.1 (3rd c.BC), “OGI” 179.18 (Egypt, 1st c.BC), etc.}}
**II**. **lay** **hold of, seize, attack**, as a disease, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 8.115, 5th c.BC: Hippocrates Medicus “Aph.” 6.51, Th. 2.51}}; of an enemy, {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Nav.” 36}}:—_passive_, ἐπείληπται νόσῳ 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Antigone” 732; τὴν αἴσθησιν ἐπιληφθείς **becoming unconscious**, {{Refs 1st c.AD+|1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Flam.” 6}}; ἐπελήφθη **had** **an epileptic fit**, {{Refs|Gal. 11.859.}}
**II.b**. of events, **overtake, surprise**, μὴ.. χειμὼν τὴν φυλακὴν ἐπιλάβοι {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 4.27; νυκτὸς ἐπιλαβούσης τὸ ἔργον [prev. work] 96; ταχὺ ἐπιλαβὸν γῆρας 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Epinomis” 974a: _impersonal_, ἐπιλαμβάνει}}, with _accusative_ et _infinitive_, **it befalls** one **that.. **, {{Refs|Paus. 6.22.4, 7.21.1.}}
**II.2**. **attain to, come** **within reach of, reach**, {{Refs|X. “An.” 6.5.6}}; ἔτη ὀκτὼ ἐ. πολέμου **live over** eight years, {{Refs 1st c.AD+|Th. 4.133; ἡμέρας ἑπτακαίδεκα τῆς ἑβδόμης ὑπατείας 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Marius” 46: with _genitive_ _partitive_, ἐ. τετάρτου μηνός}} **arrive at**, of the foetus, {{Refs|Arist. “HA” 583b22 (but ἐ. τοῦ ἑνδεκάτου μηνός, of the mother, [prev. work] 584a37)}}; ὥστε καὶ τοῦ χειμῶνος ἐ. {{Refs|Thphr. “HP” 1.9.6.}}
**II.3**. **seize, stop**, especially by pressure, τὴν ῥῖνα 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Plutus” 703; ἐ. τὸ κλύσμα τῆς ὀπίσω ὁδοῦ 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 2.87; ἐ. τὸ ὕδωρ **stop** the water-clock in court, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|Lys. 23.4, Is. 3.76; τὸν αὐλίσκον 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Ἀθηναίων Πολιτεία” 67.3, compare “Pr.” 866b13, Plb. 10.44.12; τὸ στόμα τοῖς ἐπικαλύμμασιν 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Historia Animalium” 527b21.}}
