**III.2**. **attack.** τινός {{Refs|5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Historia Graeca (Hellenica)” 4.2.22; especially with words, Pl. “Phdr.” 236b}}; of things, τῆς θερμασίας πόρων -ομένης Epieur.{{Refs|“Ep.” 2p.52U.}}; of diseases, {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Nigr.” 29.}}
**III.3**. **make a seizure of, arrest**, τῶν παίδων 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 33.9; **seize** goods in default of payment, {{Refs|[prev. author] 21.133.}}
**III.3.b**. **lay** **hands on in assertion of a claim**, {{Refs 3rd c.AD+|Pl. “Lg.” 954c, “POxy.” 1707.15 (3rd c.AD), etc.}}
**III.4**. **lay hold of, get, obtain**, προστάτεω a chief, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.127; προφάσιος ἔς τινα [prev. author] 3.36, compare 6.49; δυνάμιος [prev. author] 9.09; καιροῦ 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Lysistrata” 596}}; ἐξουσίας, γαλήνης, {{Refs 2nd c.BC+|Pl. “R.” 360d, “Plt.” 273a, compare “PTeb.” 48.20 (2nd c.BC), etc.}}; ἐ. λογισμῷ, Latin _ratione assequi_, {{Refs|Pl. “Phd.” 79a.}}
